 - Use one writer path at a time for fixes.
 - Read applicable AGENTS.md and validation guides. Before completion, verify required checks for the changed behavior even if the reviewer is clean and no fixes were needed.
-- For UI/navigation/auth/network/runtime changes, exercise affected flows with available browser tools. Recheck tool availability now; old PR comments are not evidence. Report actual checks and pending flows. CI and a clean code verdict do not substitute for required runtime validation.
+- For UI/navigation/auth/network/runtime changes, exercise affected flows on the current head. In T3 Code, start interactive checks with its built-in browser unless the user requests another browser. Discover preview_status and preview_open, check status first, and open a task tab if needed. Run any repository-required test suite with its prescribed harness. Report actual checks and pending flows. CI and a clean code verdict do not substitute for required runtime validation.
-- Review sections run sequentially on the exact selected reviewer; the host requires valid verdicts for every section plus integration coverage on the same head. An incomplete review is never approval.
+- Review sections run sequentially on the exact selected reviewer; the host requires valid verdicts for every section plus integration coverage on the same head/base/diff. Host-owned validated checkpoints resume unchanged inputs; changed reviewer, policy, prompts, head or base invalidates them. Source inspection uses an isolated committed snapshot, excluding untracked artifacts without deleting them. An incomplete review is never approval.
 - Browser scripts requiring CDP must use a compatible harness; the authenticated extension does not support newCDPSession. Keep artifacts outside the checkout or clean only task-created artifacts before review. Install missing project dependencies using its locked, prescribed environment; never bypass required checks.
-- After a reviewer failure, inspect the diagnostic and correct setup/checkout or retry the same reviewer. After automatic recovery is exhausted, report the concrete blocker and paused goal status; never silently wait for instructions.
+- After a reviewer failure, inspect its category, section and diagnostic. Transient section retries are bounded; repair setup/runtime defects before retrying the same reviewer. Exhausted review retries block approval, not independent work: continue diagnosis, CI repairs and pending validation without requesting permission. Do not pause merely for exhausted retries. Report external prerequisites and keep other work moving. Never call incomplete diagnosis an external blocker. Before ending any turn, summarize code review, CI and runtime validation separately, with exact blockers and next actions; never end silently after a failed tool. Discover browser tools from the actual tool catalog and diagnose harness setup failures before requesting user help.
 - After fixes, run focused validation, commit, and push.
 - Post a PR comment in Spanish for each pushed fix round summarizing changes and validation, preserving technical jargon in English.
 - IMPORTANT comment formatting: GitHub comments must contain real Markdown line breaks, never literal escaped sequences like \\n. Write each PR comment to a temporary .md file with a heredoc or printf that produces actual newlines, inspect the file, then post with gh pr comment ${prNumber} --body-file <file>. Do not use gh pr comment --body "...\\n..." or any command form that can render backslash-n text.
